      "en" : {
        "id" : "en",
        "terms" : {
          "gt0001" : {
            "id" : "gt0001",
            "text" : "Calcium Corrected",
            "description" : "Corrected calcium is the total calcium concentration in an individual when adjusted for the presence of hypoalbuminaemia in that individual. Because serum calcium (part of total calcium concentration) is principally bound to the plasma protein albumin, when levels of albumin are low it results in a falsely low total calcium concentration. The Payne formula performs the necessary adjustments to determine the actual total calcium concentration in individuals with hypoalbuminaemia."
          },
